Z||000000||beachbomb||01-09-2001||04:59 PM||||HI, i know some-one had posted before about where to order the Indy scoop at, could you please let me know where to order one, also, with the Indy scoop on your decklid(probably a stupid question!!)  when you open your deck-lid how does it not bump or scrap your roof? please let me know, thanks alot..jim(2 '84 Indys)||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||01-09-2001||05:42 PM||||IRM sells the scoop. There are 2 ways to mount it. One way is using the hinge/latch method that IRM gives you. The scoop is unlatched from the front and it tips towards the back on a hinge with a strut. Then you can open the decklid. On my car I remove 4 hex head screws and remove the entire scoop to open the decklid. The difference is with my mounting I have very little restriction of air and it is a very solid mount. I have heard from people that the latch isn't very good and could possibly unhook if you hit a pothole. Then the scoop would fly back and rip itself off the decklid. The last time I heard IRM changed the latch so you could pin it and it would not pop loose. If interested, I could send you pics that show how it is mounted on my car.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">   <P><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 01-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||2xsess||01-09-2001||06:27 PM||||Here's the contact info for IRM<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Lane/1588/quickcat.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Lane/1588/quickcat.html</A> <P>There is another place that makes them too<BR> <A HREF="http://www.showcars-bodyparts.com/fiero.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.showcars-bodyparts.com/fiero.html</A> <P>FOCOA also has them<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fieroowners.com/store1.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroowners.com/store1.htm</A> <P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>AOL IM : Only2xsess<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
